# Northbridge Bank · APP Scam Shield
### Stop the scam, not the customer: an end-to-end Databricks build for UK retail banking

> **Business outcome.** Since 7 Oct 2024 UK banks must reimburse authorised-push-payment (APP) scam victims, up to £85,000 per claim, with the cost split 50:50 between sending and receiving bank. That turns every scam that slips through into a direct P&L hit. On a hold-out test, Scam Shield intercepts **{{MODEL_VR}} of scam value with the same number of payment holds** as today's rules engine (**{{RULES_VR}}**). The hit-rate goes from **{{RULES_PREC}} to {{MODEL_PREC}}**, so genuine customers held per scam caught fall from {{FP_RULES}} to {{FP_MODEL}}. Every alert arrives with a GenAI case note and a Consumer-Duty-safe call script.
>
> **Value for Northbridge** (fictional bank, 2.1M current accounts): **≈{{NET_VALUE}} net per year**, made up of **{{NET_SAVING}}** of net reimbursement cost avoided plus **{{ANALYST_HOURS}} analyst hours** released, after a {{RUN_COST}} run cost. That's ROI ≈ {{ROI}}× and payback ≈ {{PAYBACK}} months. Every assumption is a row in [`northbridge_ml.business_case`](evidence/platform_queries.md#17-business-case-table).

| Who | What they get | KPI |
